# GAIA

Sustainability metrics platform. Three repos: `gaia-api` (Django), `gaia-web` (Next.js), `GAIA` (orchestration).

## Agent Routing

Workflow skills in `.claude/skills/` (`/start` proposes the next one); stack rules in one skill per code repo. Full routing: `AGENTS.md`.

| Agent / skill | Role |
|-------|------|
| `gaia-api/.agents/skills/gaia-django/` | Django rules per layer: model, service, selector, serializer, migration, test, lint |
| `gaia-web/.agents/skills/gaia-nextjs/` | Next.js rules per layer: form, table, api-layer, design, i18n key check, new module, performance |
| `sustainability-specialist` | Domain authority — LCA, RothC, regenerative metrics |
| `/architect` spec API surface | API↔Next.js contracts (OpenAPI → @hey-api/openapi-ts) |
| `/check review` | Code review on a fresh model |

## Knowledge

- Domain, product, sources: `docs/domain/`, `docs/product/`, `docs/sources/`
- References: `docs/references/README.md`
- Skills: `.claude/skills/` (workflow) and `.agents/skills/` (plane-*, penpot-design, xlsx, business-product-strategist, resolving-merge-conflicts, wizard)

## Critical Rules

1. CodeGraph first — `codegraph_context` before grep/glob
2. Contract-first — OpenAPI schema before frontend
3. PT (UX/domain), EN (code)
4. NEVER commit without authorization
5. Views never query, services never return QuerySets
